1
00:01:54,279 --> 00:02:03,969
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:04,259 --> 00:02:08,629
No living creature was hurt during
the production of this show.

3
00:03:02,287 --> 00:03:04,717
We are in the presence of my Sheik.

4
00:03:05,432 --> 00:03:06,792
I don't want to...

5
00:03:10,913 --> 00:03:13,513
cause a trouble.

6
00:03:18,181 --> 00:03:19,761
What were you doing with...

7
00:03:21,746 --> 00:03:23,896
that ring?

8
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:30,460
If you had this the whole time...

9
00:03:32,476 --> 00:03:34,886
why didn't you tell me?

10
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:42,530
I have answers...

11
00:03:43,077 --> 00:03:44,647
Osman Bey.

12
00:03:50,726 --> 00:03:53,306
We'll talk in somewhere else.

13
00:04:03,198 --> 00:04:05,168
Forgive me my Sheik.

14
00:04:05,486 --> 00:04:06,986
My Beys...

15
00:04:08,642 --> 00:04:13,372
you were not invited to...

16
00:04:15,002 --> 00:04:20,252
have greater troubles, and
become hostile to each other.

17
00:04:20,758 --> 00:04:22,938
Don't worry my Sheik.

18
00:04:23,846 --> 00:04:25,176
But...

19
00:04:26,693 --> 00:04:31,773
if you allow, I don't want to cause
a disturbance.

20
00:04:34,912 --> 00:04:38,832
Then, let it happen.

21
00:04:39,130 --> 00:04:42,730
Renew your fellowship.

22
00:04:58,089 --> 00:05:00,129
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
(In the name of Allah, the compassionate, the merciful)

23
00:05:40,173 --> 00:05:43,196
The arrow which aimed potter Idris...

24
00:05:44,766 --> 00:05:49,096
shot Osman Bey, Kumral Abdal.

25
00:05:50,631 --> 00:05:54,051
Osman Bey can remove that arrow from
his chest, my Sheik.

26
00:05:55,550 --> 00:05:58,580
But I don't know if he can stop the blood.

27
00:06:32,929 --> 00:06:35,999
- Is Osman Bey inside?
- He is, Dündar Bey.

28
00:06:46,865 --> 00:06:52,175
Umur Bey, now tell me.
Where did you find this ring?

29
00:06:52,201 --> 00:06:56,171
My daughter found this ring.

30
00:06:58,587 --> 00:07:00,096
How?

31
00:07:00,096 --> 00:07:04,056
She found it while chasing the betrayer
who killed potter Idris.

32
00:07:06,964 --> 00:07:13,224
We followed the tracks.
They led us nowhere.

33
00:07:14,964 --> 00:07:19,744
Malhun Hatun, tell me.

34
00:07:20,289 --> 00:07:23,019
Is there anything we miss?

35
00:07:24,271 --> 00:07:26,251
No Osman Bey.

36
00:07:27,586 --> 00:07:29,216
When I asked her...

37
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:35,190
She didn't tell me...

38
00:07:38,774 --> 00:07:41,074
while she has the ring, huh?

39
00:07:43,517 --> 00:07:46,328
Why did you hide this from me?

40
00:07:46,328 --> 00:07:53,268
It was obvious that the owner of the ring
was not a random man, but a Bey.

41
00:07:54,390 --> 00:07:58,155
I didn't want to put both you and her
in a difficult situation...

42
00:07:58,155 --> 00:08:00,195
before finding out what's happening.

43
00:08:00,195 --> 00:08:03,987
What are you talking about Umur Bey?
Do you know how many martyres...

44
00:08:03,987 --> 00:08:10,035
I gave, do you know how many ambushes
I got over since potter Idris died?

45
00:08:10,516 --> 00:08:15,176
Bayhoca was martyred in the ambush!

46
00:08:15,202 --> 00:08:17,362
What are you talking about?

47
00:08:18,034 --> 00:08:23,314
Both you and your daughter haven't
been friendly.

48
00:08:24,138 --> 00:08:28,668
Both friendship and hostility have
a return.

49
00:08:28,668 --> 00:08:34,408
If you had given me this ring at that time
Bayhoca wouldn't be under the dark soil now.

50
00:08:36,729 --> 00:08:42,313
You carried this while I was looking
for the betrayer.

51
00:08:42,313 --> 00:08:49,133
Osman Bey I cannot accept
your accusations!

52
00:09:46,389 --> 00:09:48,499
Can we talk Osman Bey?

53
00:09:48,634 --> 00:09:51,424
I'll see you later.

54
00:09:51,536 --> 00:09:56,306
Now go away and think of the deaths
you and your father caused.

55
00:09:56,525 --> 00:09:59,985
What kind of accusation is this,
Osman Bey? What are you trying to say?

56
00:09:59,997 --> 00:10:02,529
What about you hiding things from me?

57
00:10:02,529 --> 00:10:04,439
What did I hide from you?

58
00:10:05,519 --> 00:10:13,439
No one except for that betrayer shall face
me today so you all can dodge my anger!

59
00:10:25,292 --> 00:10:29,083
Bring me uncle Dündar.
Drag him if necessary.

60
00:10:29,083 --> 00:10:31,003
He entered the khanqah my Bey.

61
00:10:52,423 --> 00:10:54,543
Surround the khanqah.

62
00:10:54,688 --> 00:10:56,078
Find him!

63
00:10:56,281 --> 00:10:59,001
Let's go Alps!

64
00:11:03,900 --> 00:11:05,450
Check upside.

65
00:13:05,391 --> 00:13:07,511
He's gone my Bey.

66
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:11,360
- Search everywhere!
- Eyvallah (okay) my Bey.

67
00:13:11,377 --> 00:13:13,307
- Now!
- Let's go!

68
00:13:40,207 --> 00:13:42,897
Look for him everywhere!
Do not let him escape.

69
00:13:47,084 --> 00:13:49,814
Hurry up brothers!
Hurry up!

70
00:13:58,238 --> 00:14:01,018
Find Dündar Bey!
Close the exits!

71
00:14:08,511 --> 00:14:11,571
Search everywhere!

72
00:14:49,289 --> 00:14:50,839
Hurry up Alps!

73
00:15:10,004 --> 00:15:13,814
My Bey, we searched everywhere.
Dündar Bey is absent.

74
00:15:16,516 --> 00:15:17,986
Osman Bey.

75
00:15:30,153 --> 00:15:33,613
My Sheik, forgive me.

76
00:15:34,011 --> 00:15:36,031
I left untimely.

77
00:15:36,180 --> 00:15:40,380
And I had to search the khanqah.

78
00:15:42,619 --> 00:15:44,999
This was not our desire, surely.

79
00:15:45,621 --> 00:15:49,061
I understand your worries, Osman Bey.

80
00:15:49,753 --> 00:15:54,793
Obviously, you found the betrayer
who ruined you.

81
00:15:56,492 --> 00:15:59,792
Now it is time to make him pay, my Sheik.

82
00:16:18,802 --> 00:16:22,096
Boran, stay here.
Goktug, come with me.

83
00:16:22,096 --> 00:16:25,356
Alps, we are going!
Don't let anyone move!

84
00:16:34,998 --> 00:16:36,958
Hold all the exist!

85
00:16:37,505 --> 00:16:39,225
Go!

86
00:16:45,379 --> 00:16:46,969
Let's go!

87
00:17:48,333 --> 00:17:51,303
Who is that betrayer who made Osman
Bey that angry?

88
00:17:51,661 --> 00:17:54,261
He figured out whose ring it is.

89
00:17:54,298 --> 00:17:56,258
But he didn't tell me.

90
00:17:57,126 --> 00:18:00,706
He doesn't want to announce before
he captures them.

91
00:18:01,765 --> 00:18:05,155
Malhun, go to Kayı tent.

92
00:18:06,741 --> 00:18:11,141
I don't think Osman Bey would want me
there, father.

93
00:18:11,184 --> 00:18:14,834
Talk him through about why you
gave the ring to me.

94
00:18:15,766 --> 00:18:19,016
Our reasons will make him angrier.

95
00:18:19,035 --> 00:18:25,175
Yes, true but you'll learn
who the betrayer is.

96
00:18:39,116 --> 00:18:45,056
Don't tire yourself up, my Bey. My men
will carry your clothes to your home.

97
00:18:47,707 --> 00:18:49,577
- Come back again.
- Thank you.

98
00:18:49,827 --> 00:18:51,587
Come back again.

99
00:18:55,255 --> 00:19:01,525
I got excellent clothes from Konya,
for you to present your wife.

100
00:19:02,524 --> 00:19:05,884
Come, I'll give you a discount, brother.

101
00:19:06,976 --> 00:19:08,616
Have you seen Dündar Bey?

102
00:19:10,996 --> 00:19:18,366
He was here recently, but he left to see
the families of martyred Alps.

103
00:19:22,475 --> 00:19:24,505
Goodbye.

104
00:19:29,566 --> 00:19:31,986
What is happening Petrus?

105
00:19:32,931 --> 00:19:35,551
I didn't like how Boran Alp looked.

106
00:19:36,639 --> 00:19:38,939
Dündar must be in trouble.

107
00:19:39,420 --> 00:19:44,910
If Osman suspected something, that means
we're also in trouble.

108
00:19:46,861 --> 00:19:48,641
What are we going to do?

109
00:19:49,034 --> 00:19:51,014
Take precautions.

110
00:19:51,230 --> 00:19:53,850
We have to learn what's happening.

111
00:20:21,994 --> 00:20:23,924
You ordered us, Osman Bey.

112
00:20:30,359 --> 00:20:32,669
Sit first.

113
00:21:01,785 --> 00:21:03,355
This ring...

114
00:21:06,646 --> 00:21:12,246
was presented to my uncle by my father.

115
00:21:15,951 --> 00:21:20,711
Yes, it was Dündar Bey's first battle.

116
00:21:21,371 --> 00:21:24,541
Your father take it our from his finger
and gave it to his brother.

117
00:21:25,139 --> 00:21:28,289
The good old days.

118
00:21:29,086 --> 00:21:33,606
Grandmother Halime told us.
What a battle it was!

119
00:21:34,487 --> 00:21:36,395
Do you remember, brother?

120
00:21:36,395 --> 00:21:40,914
Of course I do.

121
00:21:40,914 --> 00:21:46,094
Grandmother Halime heard that uncle Dündar
was captured by the enemy in the war.

122
00:21:46,525 --> 00:21:50,695
She told everyone while she cried.

123
00:21:52,452 --> 00:21:54,272
Our hearts were shattered.

124
00:21:55,702 --> 00:22:00,532
May they be in heaven inshallah.

125
00:22:00,626 --> 00:22:03,406
- Amin.
- Amin, inshallah.

126
00:22:12,595 --> 00:22:13,835
I wish...

127
00:22:16,970 --> 00:22:20,160
my grandmother's tears
dried up...

128
00:22:21,764 --> 00:22:30,034
I wish this ring of my father was a
rope wrapped on my uncle's neck!

129
00:22:57,617 --> 00:23:00,037
What are you saying Osman Bey?

130
00:23:02,410 --> 00:23:03,770
My uncle was...

131
00:23:06,171 --> 00:23:08,691
a disappointment to my father.

132
00:23:10,410 --> 00:23:12,940
He ripped our hearts out.

133
00:23:15,231 --> 00:23:17,701
He was my grandmother's tears.

134
00:23:18,882 --> 00:23:21,792
He scratched our eyes out!

135
00:23:22,361 --> 00:23:24,991
He was my ancestors' breath!

136
00:23:25,288 --> 00:23:27,968
He took our breath away!

137
00:23:28,703 --> 00:23:37,853
All the Beys after my ancestor Oghuz
shall damn my Uncle!

138
00:23:49,027 --> 00:23:52,377
Osman Bey what is it?

139
00:23:52,975 --> 00:23:56,565
You would never curse.

140
00:23:56,963 --> 00:24:04,763
Osman Bey, the unrest is within our
ancestors including your father now.

141
00:24:06,141 --> 00:24:15,831
Osman Bey what is your tongue which shows
mercy all around the world saying?

142
00:24:17,887 --> 00:24:23,987
I wish I was speechless so I wouldn't have
said what you just heard, Bamsı Bey.

143
00:24:27,024 --> 00:24:32,194
Brother, we don't know what is happening.
Tell us.

144
00:24:38,379 --> 00:24:43,329
The betrayer who was serving both to
Papa's dogs...

145
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:47,290
and infidel Nicola...

146
00:24:50,503 --> 00:24:53,583
is my uncle Dundar Bey.

147
00:24:59,372 --> 00:25:00,992
You...

148
00:25:06,946 --> 00:25:09,516
What are you saying brother?

149
00:25:10,376 --> 00:25:13,846
Are you saying that our uncle
caused my son's death?

150
00:25:15,171 --> 00:25:17,891
This is a slander if
you don't have a proof.

151
00:25:19,940 --> 00:25:21,600
Brother.

152
00:25:25,756 --> 00:25:32,096
Uncle shot the arrow which killed
potter Idris.

153
00:25:34,975 --> 00:25:40,475
This ring fell from his bloody finger.

154
00:25:51,616 --> 00:25:54,566
He was afraid that Papa's spies
would talk.

155
00:25:55,785 --> 00:26:00,485
Then he knows them too.
He was serving them too.

156
00:26:00,944 --> 00:26:02,504
Uncle...

157
00:26:04,994 --> 00:26:07,204
Dündar...

158
00:26:08,678 --> 00:26:12,168
What am I going to do to you now?

159
00:26:18,440 --> 00:26:21,570
I want revenge Osman Bey!

160
00:26:21,816 --> 00:26:25,166
I want blood against my son's blood!

161
00:26:26,721 --> 00:26:29,001
My valiant brother.

162
00:26:29,305 --> 00:26:31,315
My mournful brother.

163
00:26:31,925 --> 00:26:38,399
Do you think my uncle's dirty blood will
relieve my grandmother's, my ancestors',

164
00:26:38,399 --> 00:26:42,441
my father's, our burning heart?

165
00:26:42,441 --> 00:26:44,181
Tell me.

166
00:26:47,103 --> 00:26:48,723
Brother.

167
00:26:52,551 --> 00:26:54,251
Brother.

168
00:27:16,494 --> 00:27:18,104
Son.

169
00:27:18,378 --> 00:27:21,118
- Bamsı Bey.
- Son.

170
00:27:22,643 --> 00:27:24,443
Beys!

171
00:27:25,782 --> 00:27:28,032
Pull yourself together!

172
00:27:38,879 --> 00:27:42,869
Brother, what are we going to do?

173
00:27:43,205 --> 00:27:47,105
How are we going to clean this dirt
on us, brother?

174
00:27:55,505 --> 00:27:58,325
My Alps are searching for him in Sogut,
brother.

175
00:27:59,160 --> 00:28:01,460
Once I got my uncle...

176
00:28:02,725 --> 00:28:05,455
Once I got him...

177
00:28:05,695 --> 00:28:07,205
But...

178
00:28:10,357 --> 00:28:13,077
no one should know about this
for now.

179
00:28:18,703 --> 00:28:27,533
Until that Dündar shows himself to us, our
swords shall remain in the scabbards.

180
00:28:32,459 --> 00:28:35,069
This is what we have to do.

181
00:28:37,390 --> 00:28:39,500
Do you understand?

182
00:28:58,415 --> 00:29:00,775
Bury the shame...

183
00:29:03,627 --> 00:29:07,277
Bury the pain in your hearts.

184
00:29:14,648 --> 00:29:21,648
When he shows up, his blood will be
halal for our valiants!

185
00:29:51,850 --> 00:29:54,039
What do you want Dündar Bey?

186
00:29:54,039 --> 00:29:56,629
I have to see Lord Nicola right now!

187
00:30:05,050 --> 00:30:08,490
You collaborated with the enemy ha?

188
00:30:08,519 --> 00:30:13,782
I did! I collaborated with Geyhatu's dogs
as well, because it led us to victory!

189
00:30:13,782 --> 00:30:19,387
Osman destroyed my army! Togay's soldiers
wiped out my remaining soldiers!

190
00:30:19,387 --> 00:30:22,174
- Is this what you call a victory?
- That's alright!

191
00:30:22,174 --> 00:30:25,334
Osman destroyed Togay's carrions!

192
00:30:25,406 --> 00:30:30,656
Osman saved you from a trouble
that you'd not be able to get rid of.

193
00:30:33,954 --> 00:30:39,659
Togay will return someday eventually.
What are we going to do then?

194
00:30:39,659 --> 00:30:41,449
Are we going to fight Mongols?

195
00:30:47,947 --> 00:30:49,837
Kalanoz.

196
00:30:51,489 --> 00:30:57,439
Before Togay comes back, we'll
go forward for our aims.

197
00:31:09,931 --> 00:31:11,691
Sogut.

198
00:31:22,335 --> 00:31:23,945
What is this?

199
00:31:24,586 --> 00:31:29,536
Papa's rats undermined Sogut.

200
00:31:32,114 --> 00:31:37,034
I made Osman lose his dignity.

201
00:31:40,182 --> 00:31:44,852
We'll enter Sogut through these tunnels...

202
00:31:46,273 --> 00:31:48,963
and we'll get out with a victory.

203
00:31:50,373 --> 00:31:53,403
This would be a golden victory, Nicola.

204
00:31:58,794 --> 00:32:04,154
- Take it to Sogut.
- Okay Bala Hatun, don't worry.

205
00:32:35,777 --> 00:32:38,147
Alaca, wait here.

206
00:32:39,336 --> 00:32:41,066
What's now, Malhun Hatun?

207
00:32:58,232 --> 00:33:00,115
Where are you going?

208
00:33:00,115 --> 00:33:02,165
I'll see Osman Bey.

209
00:33:03,681 --> 00:33:06,161
Osman Bey has a meeting with Kayı Beys.

210
00:33:10,046 --> 00:33:13,446
Okay then, I'll wait.

211
00:33:20,960 --> 00:33:24,210
Are you going to tell him your tradings
with Nicola?

212
00:33:25,340 --> 00:33:29,150
Or has Umur Bey been captured and
we have to save him?

213
00:33:33,771 --> 00:33:38,081
Bala Hatun, it's clear that you are not
here to chat.

214
00:33:38,603 --> 00:33:42,093
If you want to fight, this is not the
right place.

215
00:33:42,242 --> 00:33:49,302
I don't, Malhun Hatun I want to let you
understand you only brought us trouble.

216
00:33:51,941 --> 00:33:55,641
We didn't bring trouble. We came
in a trouble.

217
00:33:56,491 --> 00:33:59,771
Now we are working to get rid of
this trouble.

218
00:34:02,128 --> 00:34:04,388
You should know that.

219
00:34:22,033 --> 00:34:25,473
Osman Bey is available now, excuse me.

220
00:34:34,041 --> 00:34:36,941
Of course, Malhun Hatun.

221
00:34:46,236 --> 00:34:48,676
Can I come in Osman Bey?

222
00:34:49,587 --> 00:34:51,497
Come.

223
00:35:06,805 --> 00:35:11,555
Osman Bey, I am here because I respect
you being angry.

224
00:35:11,611 --> 00:35:13,971
Listen to me this time.

225
00:35:19,357 --> 00:35:23,547
You welcomed me, that's right.

226
00:35:23,922 --> 00:35:26,192
I am grateful.

227
00:35:28,338 --> 00:35:32,698
I should have brought the ring to you
as soon as I found it.

228
00:35:33,847 --> 00:35:39,167
But, feel me, Osman Bey. I am responsible
for my tribe and my father.

229
00:35:43,896 --> 00:35:47,386
I didn't want to act without
consulting him.

230
00:35:50,924 --> 00:35:57,664
But Umur Bey decided on keeping this
ring as a secret, right?

231
00:35:59,512 --> 00:36:03,882
He wanted you to show mercy if the
betrayer was one of your close ones.

232
00:36:04,497 --> 00:36:10,067
A Bey doesn't discriminate!

233
00:36:12,670 --> 00:36:18,740
The one who shows mercy to treason
betrays to the good ones!

234
00:36:27,019 --> 00:36:32,559
But you wanted to find the betrayer
before Osman Bey, ha?

235
00:36:38,142 --> 00:36:43,432
We would never give you this ring if
we wanted to ruin you Osman Bey.

236
00:36:46,028 --> 00:36:48,198
Think of it.

237
00:37:08,711 --> 00:37:11,751
Why is this Hatun here Osman Bey?

238
00:37:16,237 --> 00:37:21,087
Malhun Hatun found this ring...

239
00:37:23,289 --> 00:37:25,479
in the place where potter Idris died.

240
00:37:25,746 --> 00:37:29,246
Did she hide it so far?

241
00:37:43,456 --> 00:37:45,196
Bala Hatun.

242
00:37:50,843 --> 00:37:53,943
Who was the man Osman Bey was trying
to make talk?

243
00:37:54,202 --> 00:37:57,802
Idris. He was a potter.

244
00:37:59,202 --> 00:38:03,152
So the betrayers are in your tent.

245
00:38:03,936 --> 00:38:08,246
We were together Osman Bey.
She did this near me.

246
00:38:10,118 --> 00:38:13,088
This is Uncle Dündar's ring.

247
00:38:16,319 --> 00:38:18,249
Dündar Bey?

248
00:38:21,525 --> 00:38:23,835
Ertugrul Bey's brother...

249
00:38:24,558 --> 00:38:27,158
- Uncle Dündar's?
- Yes.

250
00:38:37,251 --> 00:38:39,791
No one must know about this.

251
00:38:40,874 --> 00:38:43,214
Hazal Hatun shouldn't hear this.

252
00:38:45,002 --> 00:38:47,542
Of course my Osman.

253
00:38:52,713 --> 00:38:54,973
Keep an eye on her.

254
00:38:55,339 --> 00:38:59,019
Invite her to meal center tomorrow.

255
00:39:02,074 --> 00:39:07,744
Hazal Hatun will lead us to uncle Dündar.

256
00:39:09,392 --> 00:39:11,332
I'll keep an eye on her.

257
00:39:11,640 --> 00:39:13,520
Don't you worry.

258
00:39:34,546 --> 00:39:36,786
Sir, Dündar Bey is here.

259
00:39:36,828 --> 00:39:38,188
Let him in.

260
00:39:41,225 --> 00:39:42,995
Who is this Turk?

261
00:39:43,921 --> 00:39:47,791
Uncle of the man who killed your brother.

262
00:39:50,184 --> 00:39:53,064
- Is this Dündar?
- Ssshhh.

263
00:39:54,025 --> 00:39:56,165
Hide your anger.

264
00:39:56,934 --> 00:39:59,344
He is my trojan horse.

265
00:40:30,980 --> 00:40:32,750
Dündar Bey...

266
00:40:33,456 --> 00:40:38,526
as you dared to come here, it must
be about something very important.

267
00:40:39,846 --> 00:40:42,246
Yes it is.

268
00:40:42,921 --> 00:40:46,221
Osman learned I killed potter Idris.

269
00:40:47,432 --> 00:40:49,532
What else did he learn?

270
00:40:49,552 --> 00:40:51,222
Isn't that enough?

271
00:40:55,240 --> 00:40:59,690
Does he know about Petrus?

272
00:40:59,801 --> 00:41:02,801
Only me so far.

273
00:41:03,335 --> 00:41:06,625
I have nowhere else to go Nicola.

274
00:41:11,761 --> 00:41:14,411
Friends are for days
like these, Dündar Bey.

275
00:41:15,793 --> 00:41:19,793
My castle is your home.

276
00:41:20,405 --> 00:41:22,295
Thank you.

277
00:41:23,242 --> 00:41:27,042
I want to take my wife Hazal
in the castle.

278
00:41:28,740 --> 00:41:30,330
Dündar Bey.

279
00:41:32,009 --> 00:41:34,229
You are a bit pale.

280
00:41:35,237 --> 00:41:37,697
Relieve, sit.

281
00:41:49,731 --> 00:41:55,976
Hazal Hatun will be my guest just like you
Dündar Bey. Don't worry.

282
00:41:55,976 --> 00:42:02,956
How? Osman killed Kalanoz's army and
Togay's soldiers.

283
00:42:05,055 --> 00:42:11,255
Dündar Bey, this is better.
Osman and I are now head to head.

284
00:42:12,554 --> 00:42:19,114
No games anymore. We both will take
what we want.

285
00:42:20,581 --> 00:42:24,361
You need to rest now.

286
00:42:25,087 --> 00:42:27,427
Commander Mikiz!

287
00:42:30,648 --> 00:42:34,628
Prepare Dündar Bey's room.
Let him rest.

288
00:43:46,582 --> 00:43:50,742
What's it, Bala Hatun?
Are you here to quarrel?

289
00:43:51,951 --> 00:43:54,171
I want to talk to you in private.

290
00:43:58,730 --> 00:44:01,000
Aren't you sick of talking, Hatun?

291
00:44:01,983 --> 00:44:06,033
Don't push it, Hatun.
I want to talk in private.

292
00:44:29,247 --> 00:44:34,117
When did you start waylaying Hatun?
What is your problem?

293
00:44:35,723 --> 00:44:37,793
You tricked me!

294
00:44:38,763 --> 00:44:41,713
You kept the ring!

295
00:44:42,587 --> 00:44:44,937
You talked about betrayers all the time.

296
00:44:45,400 --> 00:44:49,500
You asked for proof while
you're hiding it!

297
00:44:50,157 --> 00:44:52,096
I answered Osman Bey.

298
00:44:52,096 --> 00:44:58,976
If you were to answer me instead of Osman Bey,
your arrogant head would've been cut off!

299
00:45:07,161 --> 00:45:09,431
We are leaving!

300
00:45:14,122 --> 00:45:17,252
Let's go!

301
00:45:36,263 --> 00:45:40,263
Kayı Alp, how sweet you are!

302
00:45:41,567 --> 00:45:46,267
But you are useless.
You are always sleeping.

303
00:45:48,879 --> 00:45:51,159
How is my Alp sleeping?

304
00:46:06,860 --> 00:46:09,480
Mashallah (praise be)
He is growing up.

305
00:46:10,576 --> 00:46:13,166
You must have a problem, Hazal Hatun.

306
00:46:16,356 --> 00:46:18,026
Dündar Bey...

307
00:46:19,601 --> 00:46:21,281
hasn't returned.

308
00:46:22,345 --> 00:46:28,893
He told me to set dinner but he is
still absent.

309
00:46:28,893 --> 00:46:31,313
He didn't inform me either.

310
00:46:34,922 --> 00:46:39,922
At least he used to inform you when
he was going to be absent.

311
00:46:40,420 --> 00:46:42,970
He didn't even inform me!

312
00:46:43,876 --> 00:46:46,946
You don't know where he is too.

313
00:46:47,493 --> 00:46:52,703
Then I have to ask Osman Bey.

314
00:46:59,168 --> 00:47:02,258
Where is my Alp's grandfather?

315
00:47:02,702 --> 00:47:04,602
Hasn't he returned?

316
00:47:15,339 --> 00:47:18,669
What are you doing now, father?

317
00:47:21,242 --> 00:47:25,392
Osman Bey didn't speak of a name, ha?

318
00:47:27,421 --> 00:47:29,721
Osman Bey is secretive.

319
00:47:29,754 --> 00:47:35,694
He is blaming us for delivering the ring
lately instead of thanking us.

320
00:47:37,279 --> 00:47:39,229
He is hurt.

321
00:47:39,386 --> 00:47:42,206
He is right to be angry for a while.

322
00:47:42,603 --> 00:47:47,663
But his actions take us to hostility.

323
00:47:50,458 --> 00:47:52,178
Can I come in my Bey?

324
00:47:52,818 --> 00:47:54,858
Come Bahadır.

325
00:47:59,146 --> 00:48:03,196
We increased the number of Alps
around the tent, my Bey.

326
00:48:03,581 --> 00:48:06,121
Okay.
Keep your eyes open.

327
00:48:07,151 --> 00:48:10,951
Togay is like a snake.

328
00:48:11,185 --> 00:48:13,785
You cannot predict what he'll do.

329
00:48:14,476 --> 00:48:16,356
Don't worry my Bey.

330
00:48:24,672 --> 00:48:26,532
What is it Malhun?

331
00:48:27,369 --> 00:48:29,449
You seem sad.

332
00:48:31,945 --> 00:48:34,495
Osman Bey doesn't trust us.

333
00:48:35,309 --> 00:48:38,189
We did wrong to hide the ring, my Bey.

334
00:48:41,283 --> 00:48:45,693
What happened happened.
Don't worry anymore.

335
00:48:56,184 --> 00:48:58,094
Excuse me my Bey.

336
00:48:59,331 --> 00:49:02,091
Okay, go.

337
00:49:02,861 --> 00:49:06,401
Go rest, pull yourself together.

338
00:49:15,418 --> 00:49:20,808
This girl is hiding something from me.
Let's hope for the best.

339
00:49:27,332 --> 00:49:33,012
I was so offended to be infantilized,
so I waylaid her.

340
00:49:35,992 --> 00:49:38,132
What was your goal Bala?

341
00:49:41,441 --> 00:49:44,461
I wanted to call her to account
for what she did to us my Bey.

342
00:49:53,174 --> 00:49:55,624
So you wanted to call her to account.

343
00:50:00,647 --> 00:50:02,807
Can I come in Osman Bey?

344
00:50:13,379 --> 00:50:14,969
Come.

345
00:50:34,406 --> 00:50:36,356
What's it Hazal Hatun?

346
00:50:52,386 --> 00:50:56,276
We haven't heard of Dündar.

347
00:50:57,774 --> 00:51:02,904
This is not him.
Do you know anything Osman Bey?

348
00:51:04,293 --> 00:51:07,173
Who can know what you don't know?

349
00:51:17,232 --> 00:51:19,592
If you worry this lot...

350
00:51:20,951 --> 00:51:22,571
then...

351
00:51:23,665 --> 00:51:26,315
you know where Dündar Bey is.

352
00:51:33,381 --> 00:51:35,771
I don't know, Osman Bey.

353
00:51:37,110 --> 00:51:40,390
Why would I ask you if I knew?

354
00:51:48,369 --> 00:51:50,209
So you don't know?

355
00:52:02,593 --> 00:52:06,553
Hazal Hatun, come to the meal center
with me tomorrow.

356
00:52:06,664 --> 00:52:11,784
I'll need help. Also you'd let yourself
a while.

357
00:52:16,951 --> 00:52:18,571
Okay.

358
00:52:19,734 --> 00:52:21,854
Sure, Bala Hatun.

359
00:52:22,108 --> 00:52:27,948
We'll eventually
hear about him here in Sogut.

360
00:52:30,881 --> 00:52:32,911
Can I come in my Bey?

361
00:52:33,727 --> 00:52:35,757
Come.

362
00:52:53,164 --> 00:52:55,934
She doesn't know where Dündar Bey is.

363
00:52:57,005 --> 00:53:03,135
All she is worried about is the things
they did behind my back.

364
00:53:09,839 --> 00:53:11,229
Tell me.

365
00:53:11,411 --> 00:53:16,021
We investigated, my Bey.
No one saw Dündar Bey.

366
00:53:16,683 --> 00:53:18,633
He is out of Sogut, apparently.

367
00:53:21,058 --> 00:53:26,318
He won't get away from my wrath even
if he goes to the far end of the world!

368
00:53:31,744 --> 00:53:34,408
Watch Dündar Bey's tent.

369
00:53:34,408 --> 00:53:36,858
- Eyvallah (okay) my Bey.
- Command is yours my Bey.

370
00:53:47,603 --> 00:53:50,313
We'll talk about your issue later Bala.

371
00:53:53,586 --> 00:53:57,776
Keep an eye on Hazal Hatun for now.

372
00:53:59,582 --> 00:54:01,572
She'll lead us to my uncle.

373
00:54:02,587 --> 00:54:04,367
Don't worry my Bey.

374
00:54:07,520 --> 00:54:09,170
Excuse me.

375
00:54:47,630 --> 00:54:49,840
From a sea to another.

376
00:54:50,193 --> 00:54:52,693
This latter is for Papa.

377
00:55:21,166 --> 00:55:23,526
Dündar's mask has fallen.

378
00:55:24,773 --> 00:55:26,523
He went to Nicola.

379
00:55:27,209 --> 00:55:30,529
Osman must have suspected him.

380
00:55:31,930 --> 00:55:34,280
We are safe for now.

381
00:55:38,530 --> 00:55:40,400
Hazal Hatun.

382
00:55:42,371 --> 00:55:48,561
She is still a threat to us. Dündar must
have told her about us. Where is she?

383
00:55:48,849 --> 00:55:55,649
She is in the tent, but if she had talked,
Osman would have found us by now.

384
00:55:56,337 --> 00:55:58,967
We have to kill her before she speaks!

385
00:55:59,478 --> 00:56:01,188
There's no another way.

386
00:56:15,387 --> 00:56:18,632
May Allah bless you.
May Allah bless you.

387
00:56:18,632 --> 00:56:20,582
Enjoy your meal.

388
00:56:24,618 --> 00:56:27,408
- May Allah bless you.
- Enjoy your meal.

389
00:56:28,187 --> 00:56:30,307
May Allah bless you, daughter.

390
00:56:44,200 --> 00:56:49,280
Mother Fatma, has your daughter Irmak
healed? Does she need anything?

391
00:56:49,332 --> 00:56:53,160
She has food thanks to you Bala Hatun.
Her blood renewed.

392
00:56:53,160 --> 00:56:54,865
May Allah bless you.

393
00:56:54,865 --> 00:56:57,385
Masha Allah (praise be).

394
00:56:59,798 --> 00:57:02,328
I will come to your house.

395
00:57:02,328 --> 00:57:04,205
I'll salute Irmak.

396
00:57:04,205 --> 00:57:07,355
Of course. You are most welcome.

397
00:57:08,055 --> 00:57:12,675
Gonca, let's go to Mother Fatma's.

398
00:57:16,949 --> 00:57:18,609
Let's go.

399
00:57:20,649 --> 00:57:22,389
Wait a minute mother.

400
00:57:24,462 --> 00:57:26,132
Hazal Hatun.

401
00:57:27,607 --> 00:57:29,997
We are going Mother Fatma's.

402
00:57:30,141 --> 00:57:32,371
Can you manage here?

403
00:57:32,900 --> 00:57:38,090
Of course. I got it. You can go.

404
00:57:38,514 --> 00:57:40,024
Thank you.

405
00:57:41,429 --> 00:57:42,999
Let's go.

406
00:57:51,234 --> 00:57:53,294
Ayse Hatun.

407
00:57:57,454 --> 00:58:01,534
We are going to the bazaar to
buy cloth.

408
00:58:01,557 --> 00:58:04,277
- Let's go.
- Okay my Hanım.

409
00:58:38,964 --> 00:58:43,724
Osman Bey was right. Hazal Hatun was
waiting for us to leave.

410
00:58:50,235 --> 00:58:53,078
Let Boran Alp know Gonca.
Go now.

411
00:58:53,078 --> 00:58:54,918
Okay Bala.

412
00:59:09,124 --> 00:59:11,334
Hazal Hatun is coming here.

413
00:59:13,141 --> 00:59:17,411
- Is she alone?
- She is with a helper Hatun.

414
00:59:19,464 --> 00:59:22,454
We can't kill her today.
It'll draw attention.

415
00:59:24,571 --> 00:59:26,291
What are we going to do?

416
00:59:37,494 --> 00:59:42,524
Where is my Dündar Bey?
Do you know?

417
00:59:42,894 --> 00:59:46,784
We haven't seen him since yesterday.

418
00:59:47,450 --> 00:59:51,536
I have quality clothes from Konya.
If you want to have a look...

419
00:59:51,536 --> 00:59:54,256
Don't play with me Petrus.

420
00:59:58,589 --> 01:00:00,639
I know who you are.

421
01:00:07,057 --> 01:00:10,547
Where is my man, Dündar Bey?

422
01:00:12,242 --> 01:00:14,132
What is happening?

423
01:00:18,719 --> 01:00:21,449
What is happening in this sinister town?

424
01:00:33,113 --> 01:00:36,319
Has anyone followed you on your
way here Hazal Hatun?

425
01:00:36,319 --> 01:00:40,459
No.
What is happening?

426
01:00:43,344 --> 01:00:45,904
Dündar Bey refuged to Nicola.

427
01:01:00,681 --> 01:01:02,371
Osman.

428
01:01:08,641 --> 01:01:11,571
How did he know?

429
01:01:12,366 --> 01:01:17,136
We just got informed Hazal Hatun.

430
01:01:17,341 --> 01:01:21,101
Osman is looking for
Dündar Bey everywhere.

431
01:01:22,596 --> 01:01:25,796
He doesn't suspect you, obviously.

432
01:01:29,077 --> 01:01:32,477
At least for now.

433
01:01:41,829 --> 01:01:44,229
You didn't like this cloth.

434
01:01:47,187 --> 01:01:51,867
Did he just leave me and run off?

435
01:01:53,891 --> 01:01:59,651
Dündar Bey had a plan for a situation
lilke this?

436
01:02:01,450 --> 01:02:02,980
Plan?

437
01:02:04,787 --> 01:02:06,727
What kind of plan?

438
01:02:07,225 --> 01:02:12,255
We are prepared. Don't worry.
Be calm.

439
01:02:13,735 --> 01:02:17,855
- I can't go back to the tent.
- We'll take you to Dündar Bey.

440
01:02:19,080 --> 01:02:22,948
Get rid of the Hatun with you and
come to Boztepe.

441
01:02:22,948 --> 01:02:27,868
No, I have to go back to the tent.

442
01:02:29,167 --> 01:02:33,697
I must take my goods, my ornament...

443
01:02:33,697 --> 01:02:35,097
Never!

444
01:02:36,294 --> 01:02:42,054
We don't have time for this. Osman will
chase you if he learns where Dündar is.

445
01:02:43,869 --> 01:02:47,009
Now go.
Now.

446
01:03:52,413 --> 01:03:57,423
We bury her.
No one will find her.

447
01:04:29,552 --> 01:04:33,312
She is confused, apparently She's trying
to figure out what she's going to do.

448
01:04:36,623 --> 01:04:39,823
What are you looking at Boran Alp?
Why are you surprised?

449
01:04:41,793 --> 01:04:43,433
Let's go.

450
01:04:55,698 --> 01:04:57,368
Where are Alps?

451
01:05:02,121 --> 01:05:04,731
Aren't we returning to the meal center,
my Hanım?

452
01:05:05,765 --> 01:05:10,825
You return to the tent.
I have things to do.

453
01:05:15,225 --> 01:05:17,155
I'll inform Osman Bey.

454
01:05:17,616 --> 01:05:20,306
Brother, follow her.

455
01:05:22,873 --> 01:05:25,493
Let's go my Gonca, let's go.

456
01:05:51,072 --> 01:05:53,902
This is enough to cover her sins.

457
01:05:54,180 --> 01:05:56,250
What about Dündar?

458
01:05:56,279 --> 01:06:00,289
Dündar is still a big threat for us.

459
01:06:00,426 --> 01:06:02,306
His turn will come.

460
01:06:27,769 --> 01:06:30,059
Come on. Let's leave.

461
01:06:40,212 --> 01:06:41,902
What is this hole for?

462
01:06:43,888 --> 01:06:49,608
Dündar Bey entrusted us gold and some
papers in case he runs off.

463
01:06:50,325 --> 01:06:54,585
He told us to give them to you.

464
01:06:55,548 --> 01:06:57,538
All in this hole.

465
01:07:06,252 --> 01:07:08,622
This hole is empty.

466
01:07:12,570 --> 01:07:15,324
What are you doing?

467
01:07:15,324 --> 01:07:18,504
Everyone gets what they deserve!

468
01:07:26,043 --> 01:07:29,113
Let me go.
Let me go!

469
01:07:30,380 --> 01:07:33,240
Why are you doing this?
Let me go!

470
01:07:34,004 --> 01:07:39,544
Your reason of death is betraying
your people.

471
01:07:42,512 --> 01:07:46,302
Sir Petrus, shall I end her?

472
01:07:47,748 --> 01:07:49,598
End her.

473
01:07:51,308 --> 01:07:53,738
No!

474
01:08:06,202 --> 01:08:08,557
Damn it! Osman!

475
01:08:08,557 --> 01:08:10,307
Run Petrus!

476
01:08:32,996 --> 01:08:37,726
I'd love to bury you alive,
you should thank to my Bey.

477
01:08:40,158 --> 01:08:41,918
Get out.

478
01:09:31,257 --> 01:09:34,357
You'll tell everything!

479
01:09:35,613 --> 01:09:40,779
Being silent is the
biggest pray, Savcı Bey.

480
01:09:42,779 --> 01:09:48,489
I know how to make you talk.
Are you working for Papa...

481
01:09:48,519 --> 01:09:50,809
or Nicola dog?

482
01:09:51,640 --> 01:09:53,220
Take him!

483
01:10:21,120 --> 01:10:24,810
So you are the head of evil, huh?

484
01:10:24,885 --> 01:10:26,615
Right?!

485
01:10:27,182 --> 01:10:29,572
So, you are Petros, huh?

486
01:10:30,153 --> 01:10:33,253
What about Süleyman that my
father mentioned?

487
01:10:34,668 --> 01:10:36,818
Where is Melik the merchant?

488
01:10:37,433 --> 01:10:39,593
Tell me!

489
01:10:43,349 --> 01:10:45,999
They are decaying under the soil.

490
01:10:48,921 --> 01:10:52,041
Now it's my turn.

491
01:10:53,085 --> 01:10:56,385
Come on, kill me!
Kill me!

492
01:10:57,111 --> 01:11:01,101
Petros, huh?
Petros...

493
01:11:04,693 --> 01:11:10,373
You won't die that easy.
We'll have some conversations, Süleyman.

494
01:11:17,697 --> 01:11:22,007
You can call me Petros.

495
01:11:33,945 --> 01:11:36,075
Petros, huh?

496
01:12:50,008 --> 01:12:57,228
Hazal Hatun of Çobanoğullar,
sister to a valiant brother.

497
01:13:01,169 --> 01:13:03,759
Did you provoke my uncle
all this time?

498
01:13:05,913 --> 01:13:09,803
Sooner or later...

499
01:13:11,642 --> 01:13:14,782
...you will face your end, Osman Bey.

500
01:13:21,393 --> 01:13:23,563
Take them away.

501
01:14:03,130 --> 01:14:05,660
Osman Bey captured Hazal Hatun.

502
01:14:07,765 --> 01:14:09,875
Let's greet them, Gonca.

503
01:14:45,601 --> 01:14:47,561
What did they do?

504
01:14:47,651 --> 01:14:49,571
O' people!

505
01:14:51,208 --> 01:14:58,858
These are the low people who
worked with the traitors in our tribe!

506
01:14:59,817 --> 01:15:05,597
Traitors! Burn in hell!
God damn you!

507
01:15:07,561 --> 01:15:11,041
We caught Hazal Hatun running away
with them.

508
01:15:12,014 --> 01:15:14,554
How can Hazal Hatun do that?

509
01:15:20,310 --> 01:15:28,210
I found out who the traitor who
deceived many of our alps.

510
01:15:31,379 --> 01:15:37,959
This is the darkest day of mine.

511
01:15:43,807 --> 01:15:50,697
The traitor of our tribe is
someone from my own blood...

512
01:15:53,672 --> 01:15:56,322
...my uncle Dündar Bey!

513
01:16:11,304 --> 01:16:18,034
He will be caught soon and get
punished as he deserves.

514
01:16:18,754 --> 01:16:20,464
Father...

515
01:16:21,930 --> 01:16:23,960
Father...

516
01:16:23,979 --> 01:16:26,489
What did you do...

517
01:16:27,376 --> 01:16:32,156
Take Hazal Hatun to the tent.

518
01:16:34,497 --> 01:16:36,617
And put guards at her tent.

519
01:16:41,555 --> 01:16:46,545
She won't leave there before
my uncle Dündar get's captured.

520
01:16:48,484 --> 01:16:53,714
And after he gets caught, send
her to her family.

521
01:16:57,761 --> 01:17:03,541
She will never step into my lands
in my lifetime.

522
01:17:05,252 --> 01:17:06,922
Come on.

523
01:17:20,655 --> 01:17:23,215
Take these two to the caged tent.

524
01:18:03,307 --> 01:18:05,157
Osman Bey.

525
01:18:09,089 --> 01:18:10,489
I told you that...

526
01:18:13,417 --> 01:18:15,497
...even if the traitor is
my father...

527
01:18:16,635 --> 01:18:19,785
...his blood is halal for you.

528
01:18:27,456 --> 01:18:31,186
Let it be as the laws say.

529
01:18:35,929 --> 01:18:39,469
Let there be no traitor
left in our tribe.

530
01:18:44,705 --> 01:18:47,475
Don't feel ashamed, Aygül.

531
01:18:49,148 --> 01:18:54,038
Children can't suffer for their
fathers' sins.

532
01:18:57,130 --> 01:18:59,640
You are a crown on our heads.

533
01:19:01,924 --> 01:19:09,394
It is my uncle Dündar Bey who should
feel ashamed.

534
01:19:59,531 --> 01:20:02,281
Brother...
Brother...

535
01:20:07,719 --> 01:20:15,909
Let us start from the beginning then.
You led the Cumans here to get documents.

536
01:20:18,097 --> 01:20:20,947
And my uncle Dündar helped you, huh?

537
01:20:27,161 --> 01:20:32,151
Why did you try to bury Hazal Hatun alive?

538
01:20:54,474 --> 01:21:01,204
When Dündar's treachery got revealed, you
wanted to kill her who knows everything.

539
01:21:05,124 --> 01:21:07,184
Right?

540
01:21:14,618 --> 01:21:18,448
When Osman Bey questions,
you will answer.

541
01:21:40,682 --> 01:21:46,522
Hazal Hatun knew that you serve the pope,
that you are allied with Nikola against me.

542
01:21:48,571 --> 01:21:51,581
You were scared to get revealed,
didn't you?

543
01:21:55,802 --> 01:22:01,982
If you know everything,
what do you want from us?

544
01:22:05,334 --> 01:22:07,994
I want Dündar! Dündar!

545
01:22:16,399 --> 01:22:18,619
Where is Dündar?

546
01:22:21,046 --> 01:22:22,626
Where?

547
01:22:25,532 --> 01:22:28,172
Why should I tell you this?

548
01:22:31,328 --> 01:22:36,078
Why should I tell you where
your uncle...

549
01:22:37,771 --> 01:22:41,111
...who cause the death of
Bayhoca...

550
01:22:44,019 --> 01:22:45,739
...and...

551
01:22:46,527 --> 01:22:52,177
...many of your alps for
your throne?

552
01:22:52,329 --> 01:22:56,459
Why should I waste a useful
ally like him?

553
01:22:57,360 --> 01:23:02,850
He will be a trouble for you and
the Turkish tribes as long as he is alive.

554
01:23:03,652 --> 01:23:07,772
Why should I tell you where
a traitor hides, Osman Bey?

555
01:23:10,800 --> 01:23:14,530
My question is simple, Petros.
Very simple.

556
01:23:15,386 --> 01:23:19,036
You will stay alive until Dündar dies.

557
01:23:21,699 --> 01:23:25,489
As long as he breathes,
you will want to die.

558
01:23:26,140 --> 01:23:29,283
As long as he breathes,
you will get tortured...

559
01:23:29,283 --> 01:23:31,883
...you will want to die.

560
01:23:31,984 --> 01:23:37,824
Now, tell me where Dündar is.

561
01:23:40,104 --> 01:23:41,794
Where?

562
01:23:43,529 --> 01:23:48,569
Petros, tell him.
Tell him...

563
01:23:48,891 --> 01:23:53,871
Dündar Bey is over.
What good can his life do?

564
01:23:55,145 --> 01:23:59,075
Osman Bey knows everything now.

565
01:24:00,145 --> 01:24:02,345
We lost.

566
01:24:10,072 --> 01:24:15,682
Let it end now.
I want to die, that's all. Tell him.

567
01:24:31,712 --> 01:24:33,352
Nikola.

568
01:24:37,298 --> 01:24:42,958
Dündar took refuge in Nikola.

569
01:25:23,326 --> 01:25:25,726
Get out of my way.

570
01:25:27,630 --> 01:25:30,020
You know Osman Bey's order, Aygül.

571
01:25:30,710 --> 01:25:34,720
I'm the last person to run
over Osman Bey's orders, Cerkutay.

572
01:25:34,993 --> 01:25:37,593
I have some things to say.

573
01:25:47,944 --> 01:25:49,754
Don't waste time.

574
01:26:14,292 --> 01:26:17,352
You did everything together, didn't you?

575
01:26:17,471 --> 01:26:22,531
You are in treachery since the day that
my father couldn't be the bey.

576
01:26:22,583 --> 01:26:26,373
It is your father who betrays,
not me.

577
01:26:27,981 --> 01:26:31,511
Dündar Bey son of Süleyman Shah.

578
01:26:32,752 --> 01:26:35,852
Your father.

579
01:26:36,755 --> 01:26:42,375
A Kayı bey.
I'm of the Çobanoğulları.

580
01:26:43,566 --> 01:26:46,726
I'm not a traitor.

581
01:26:47,105 --> 01:26:50,975
You never felt that you belonged
to this tribe.

582
01:26:53,445 --> 01:26:57,365
It is you who fed my father
with treason.

583
01:26:58,070 --> 01:27:03,810
I've put effort for him to
act like a man...

584
01:27:03,964 --> 01:27:10,314
...but it was her daughter
who acted like a man.

585
01:27:11,794 --> 01:27:13,674
Not him.

586
01:27:18,672 --> 01:27:23,402
My revenge for my mother
is coming, Hazal Hatun.

587
01:27:24,341 --> 01:27:28,191
Don't think that it's over.

588
01:27:29,003 --> 01:27:30,453
So?

589
01:27:31,715 --> 01:27:33,835
What are you waiting for?

590
01:27:35,336 --> 01:27:38,046
Get your revenge.

591
01:27:58,730 --> 01:28:00,630
Thank Osman Bey.

592
01:28:06,258 --> 01:28:11,638
If it wasn't for his order,
it would be your head falling.

593
01:28:12,815 --> 01:28:15,365
Hazal Hatun.

594
01:28:44,704 --> 01:28:48,674
I couldn't cut your throat...

595
01:28:49,128 --> 01:28:52,268
...like I cut your mother's...

596
01:28:53,505 --> 01:28:55,785
Aygül...

597
01:28:56,336 --> 01:28:58,256
...that's why I'm sad.

598
01:29:07,914 --> 01:29:11,194
We found out who is the murderer
of your brother, Ertuğrul.

599
01:29:13,783 --> 01:29:17,833
It was Dündar Bey who caused
him to die in that ambush.

600
01:29:22,684 --> 01:29:25,594
Shame on you Dündar Bey.

601
01:29:27,004 --> 01:29:29,394
Shame on you.

602
01:29:46,154 --> 01:29:48,684
Is it true, Savcı Bey?

603
01:29:58,412 --> 01:30:00,282
It's true, my wife.

604
01:30:06,039 --> 01:30:09,419
The traitor is my uncle.

605
01:30:23,728 --> 01:30:25,628
Where is that traitor?

606
01:30:26,088 --> 01:30:28,888
Where did he go to?

607
01:30:29,942 --> 01:30:32,542
It's a matter of time to
find him.

608
01:30:37,665 --> 01:30:41,985
For him to get caught and
die in my hands.

609
01:30:42,130 --> 01:30:43,960
It's a matter of time.

610
01:32:00,157 --> 01:32:03,007
You know best what you feel, Aygül.

611
01:32:05,749 --> 01:32:07,789
I can't.

612
01:32:15,119 --> 01:32:17,579
I don't even remember the faces of mine.

613
01:32:18,515 --> 01:32:23,195
What does mother mean?
What does father mean?

614
01:32:24,770 --> 01:32:27,130
I never knew.

615
01:32:29,814 --> 01:32:32,324
I wish I never knew as well.

616
01:32:34,513 --> 01:32:38,523
That sinister Hazal Hatun killed
my mother.

617
01:32:40,357 --> 01:32:43,567
I live with her in this tribe for months.

618
01:32:47,896 --> 01:32:51,306
Another person I live with
in this tribe...

619
01:32:51,805 --> 01:32:53,195
...I mean...

620
01:32:55,517 --> 01:32:57,287
...my father...

621
01:33:00,670 --> 01:33:03,590
...will get killed by
Osman Bey.

622
01:33:04,750 --> 01:33:07,450
For being a traitor.

623
01:33:12,085 --> 01:33:14,385
You are right, Cerkutay.

624
01:33:17,630 --> 01:33:20,730
I know best how I feel.

625
01:33:40,321 --> 01:33:42,281
I'm with you.

626
01:33:45,393 --> 01:33:48,393
I'll do anything to console you.

627
01:33:51,304 --> 01:33:53,524
I know, you are mad at me.

628
01:33:54,027 --> 01:33:56,537
Even though I don't know why.

629
01:33:57,465 --> 01:34:02,465
But if you want to talk about it...

630
01:34:22,112 --> 01:34:24,622
You understand me the best...

631
01:34:24,861 --> 01:34:26,431
...Cerkutay.

632
01:34:48,367 --> 01:34:50,392
May I enter, my bey?

633
01:34:50,392 --> 01:34:52,342
Come.

634
01:34:56,609 --> 01:34:58,771
-Any news?
-My bey.

635
01:34:58,771 --> 01:35:01,441
We know who the traitor is.

636
01:35:01,930 --> 01:35:03,590
Who is it?

637
01:35:03,654 --> 01:35:05,304
Dündar Bey.

638
01:35:05,727 --> 01:35:07,957
Dündar Bey, huh?

639
01:35:09,251 --> 01:35:11,151
It was clear.

640
01:35:12,880 --> 01:35:16,430
It was clear that someone who
enters Osman Bey's tent.

641
01:35:17,283 --> 01:35:19,705
Where is Dündar Bey?

642
01:35:19,705 --> 01:35:24,144
He isn't around, my bey.
Osman Bey and his alps are searching.

643
01:35:24,144 --> 01:35:25,974
It seems that he is in hiding.

644
01:35:25,974 --> 01:35:29,758
He must've taken refuge in whoever
he was working for.

645
01:35:30,019 --> 01:35:34,559
You worked well, Bahadır.
Find out where Dündar Bey is.

646
01:35:35,015 --> 01:35:38,865
Let me know at once if Osman Bey
captures him.

647
01:35:39,192 --> 01:35:41,252
As you order, my bey.

648
01:35:52,672 --> 01:35:56,632
Look at what Dündar Bey did...

649
01:36:01,761 --> 01:36:03,231
Uncle!

650
01:36:09,001 --> 01:36:10,791
Uncle!

651
01:36:14,372 --> 01:36:16,412
My uncle is with Nikola.

652
01:36:17,310 --> 01:36:18,550
From now on...

653
01:36:19,782 --> 01:36:22,572
I know what's necessary to do.

654
01:36:24,285 --> 01:36:28,285
We will send a messenger and we will
take my uncle from them...

655
01:36:29,493 --> 01:36:31,583
in return for ransom money.

656
01:36:32,200 --> 01:36:35,010
I want to go, Osman Bey.

657
01:36:36,517 --> 01:36:38,617
You are angry now.

658
01:36:40,318 --> 01:36:42,498
You are angry.

659
01:36:43,460 --> 01:36:45,760
I don't want you to see Nikola and...

660
01:36:46,115 --> 01:36:50,345
I don't want you to see my uncle.

661
01:36:53,832 --> 01:36:55,602
What's best is...

662
01:37:00,113 --> 01:37:03,573
that Gündüz brother should go.

663
01:37:07,214 --> 01:37:09,944
This is better, brother.

664
01:37:13,825 --> 01:37:15,335
Brother...

665
01:37:15,636 --> 01:37:17,866
it's your responsibility.

666
01:37:18,907 --> 01:37:21,387
We will give them everything they want.

667
01:37:21,661 --> 01:37:25,661
However, not our lands.

668
01:37:27,297 --> 01:37:31,537
They will want so many things, Osman Bey.

669
01:37:32,051 --> 01:37:34,611
Goods or property don't matter.

670
01:37:34,799 --> 01:37:37,879
I just want to get through this.

671
01:37:38,164 --> 01:37:41,054
We will make everything up.

672
01:37:45,544 --> 01:37:50,234
Savcı brother. Bayhoca's killer suffered
the consequences.

673
01:37:50,555 --> 01:37:53,235
Now we know why.

674
01:37:55,286 --> 01:37:56,396
He...

675
01:37:57,692 --> 01:38:00,132
will pay for it.

676
01:38:01,012 --> 01:38:03,052
Don't worry.

677
01:38:03,599 --> 01:38:06,309
I will feel better, brother.

678
01:38:06,860 --> 01:38:09,130
I will feel better.

679
01:38:09,448 --> 01:38:16,248
However, when Nikola dies
too, I will be more comfortable.

680
01:38:16,297 --> 01:38:20,297
- Inshallah.
- Inshallah.

681
01:38:33,855 --> 01:38:37,305
I managed to step in Söğüt.

682
01:38:37,504 --> 01:38:40,354
The tunnels shown on the map...

683
01:38:41,070 --> 01:38:42,310
are real.

684
01:38:42,964 --> 01:38:47,244
Petrus's shop, the church and the inn.
They are all connected.

685
01:38:49,104 --> 01:38:53,994
I should confess
that I hated your tricks, Nikola.

686
01:38:54,465 --> 01:38:59,915
Now, I see that you are going to win a
victory thanks to your political wisdom.

687
01:39:01,558 --> 01:39:04,428
Söğüt is ours now.

688
01:39:05,225 --> 01:39:08,255
No one will prevent that.

689
01:39:08,624 --> 01:39:10,754
What's your plan, Nikola?

690
01:39:16,443 --> 01:39:18,163
Gündüz Bey is here.

691
01:39:19,969 --> 01:39:26,229
So, Osman knows Dündar Bey is here.

692
01:39:27,355 --> 01:39:29,025
Let him in.

693
01:39:56,653 --> 01:39:58,153
Gündüz Bey.

694
01:39:59,825 --> 01:40:03,595
Where is Dündar Bey?

695
01:40:05,165 --> 01:40:09,465
- What are you talking about?
- Stop playing with me.

696
01:40:10,460 --> 01:40:13,530
I know that the traitor is here.

697
01:40:13,669 --> 01:40:16,169
Listen to me carefully.

698
01:40:16,413 --> 01:40:19,543
Give him to me.

699
01:40:21,293 --> 01:40:26,433
Why would I give a loyal man like
Dündar Bey to you?

700
01:40:26,656 --> 01:40:29,396
You're done with him, that's why.

701
01:40:29,641 --> 01:40:33,641
He is someone disreputable now.

702
01:40:34,939 --> 01:40:36,349
And...

703
01:40:37,412 --> 01:40:39,662
he is a disgrace of Kayıs.

704
01:40:44,603 --> 01:40:48,603
Osman dreams of a bloody end, obviously.

705
01:40:49,399 --> 01:40:52,149
As every traitor has a bloody end.

706
01:40:53,004 --> 01:40:55,514
So, Gündüz Bey...

707
01:40:56,218 --> 01:40:59,618
what do you offer for Dündar Bey?

708
01:41:00,823 --> 01:41:02,553
Ransom.

709
01:41:04,039 --> 01:41:06,949
A thousand gold coins.

710
01:41:10,147 --> 01:41:11,747
So...

711
01:41:12,387 --> 01:41:15,757
this is my worth.

712
01:41:21,929 --> 01:41:25,769
The traitor is here.

713
01:41:41,140 --> 01:41:43,370
The traitor is here.

714
01:41:45,678 --> 01:41:47,178
Traitor?

715
01:41:48,433 --> 01:41:50,423
Traitor?

716
01:41:53,442 --> 01:41:54,862
Osman...

717
01:41:55,933 --> 01:41:59,033
treated me as if I'm nobody...

718
01:42:00,012 --> 01:42:02,672
in the lands that I and my brother took.

719
01:42:04,197 --> 01:42:11,227
He endangered everything we took.

720
01:42:12,193 --> 01:42:14,523
He took possession of our tent.

721
01:42:15,110 --> 01:42:19,110
He took my deserved Beyhood from me.

722
01:42:20,073 --> 01:42:24,223
We are surrounded by
enemies because of him.

723
01:42:24,975 --> 01:42:28,275
Your eyes are still closed, Gündüz.

724
01:42:28,467 --> 01:42:31,267
Wake up, Gündüz!

725
01:42:32,759 --> 01:42:36,759
If there's a traitor in
the tent, it's not me.

726
01:42:37,356 --> 01:42:39,246
It's Osman.

727
01:42:47,588 --> 01:42:48,758
Uncle.

728
01:42:49,806 --> 01:42:52,016
When I looked at your eyes...

729
01:42:53,332 --> 01:42:56,432
I used to see my father.

730
01:42:58,473 --> 01:43:01,443
When I looked at your face...

731
01:43:02,439 --> 01:43:07,469
I used to see the beautiful face of
my grandmother, Hayme Mother.

732
01:43:10,611 --> 01:43:14,391
What did you do to yourself, uncle?

733
01:43:14,429 --> 01:43:17,719
Tell me. What did you do to yourself?

734
01:43:17,757 --> 01:43:21,887
How could you betray our
family and traditions?

735
01:43:21,946 --> 01:43:25,336
How could you? Tell me, father!

736
01:43:25,631 --> 01:43:28,171
How!

737
01:43:28,467 --> 01:43:36,757
I protect my family and
traditions in my heart!

738
01:43:37,241 --> 01:43:40,731
Don't worry.

739
01:43:41,162 --> 01:43:42,932
Don't worry.

740
01:43:44,238 --> 01:43:51,268
I won't let Geyhatu take over these lands
that my brother Ertuğrul Ghazi took.

741
01:43:51,648 --> 01:43:57,128
I won't let our Alps die...

742
01:43:57,481 --> 01:44:00,751
because of Osman.

743
01:44:08,231 --> 01:44:10,141
Bravo!

744
01:44:12,313 --> 01:44:13,773
Bravo!

745
01:44:16,410 --> 01:44:18,250
Bravo!

746
01:44:20,327 --> 01:44:23,777
When I look at your face now...

747
01:44:24,338 --> 01:44:31,568
Let me tell you what I think of when I
look at your ambitious eyes, uncle.

748
01:44:31,937 --> 01:44:33,687
Tell me.

749
01:44:34,657 --> 01:44:36,457
A miserable person.

750
01:44:37,029 --> 01:44:39,279
A traitor...

751
01:44:40,134 --> 01:44:46,824
who is ambitious and who is the reason
for our Alps' death.

752
01:44:53,618 --> 01:44:57,298
That's enough.

753
01:45:03,112 --> 01:45:09,812
It just hurts me to see...

754
01:45:09,974 --> 01:45:13,044
the relatives hating each other.

755
01:45:21,143 --> 01:45:23,893
My Alps will be waiting for
you next to the Castle...

756
01:45:24,677 --> 01:45:30,227
with a thousand gold coins.

757
01:45:32,694 --> 01:45:36,554
Think wisely, Nikola.
A thousand gold coins...

758
01:45:37,754 --> 01:45:40,144
will be yours with just an order of yours.

759
01:45:40,228 --> 01:45:43,628
I love generous offers.

760
01:45:51,839 --> 01:45:57,269
Your offer made me happy but
Dündar Bey is my guest.

761
01:45:59,354 --> 01:46:02,154
He will stay here as long as he wants.

762
01:46:02,836 --> 01:46:05,176
The gold coins that Osman
will give can't buy...

763
01:46:05,249 --> 01:46:10,479
the peace that Dündar Bey and
I set up here, Gündüz Bey.

764
01:46:16,602 --> 01:46:22,482
So, I am not giving you Dündar Bey.

765
01:46:22,604 --> 01:46:25,954
I send my regards to Osman Bey.

766
01:46:33,437 --> 01:46:37,797
The day you die will be our feast day.

767
01:46:47,255 --> 01:46:51,525
The day you
die will be our feast day, uncle!

768
01:47:01,719 --> 01:47:04,039
Dündar Bey...

769
01:47:05,988 --> 01:47:08,528
you should rest.

770
01:47:10,199 --> 01:47:15,929
We will be in peace here soon.

771
01:47:33,518 --> 01:47:36,368
Söğüt is already ours.

772
01:47:36,848 --> 01:47:41,778
Dündar is a traitor. He doesn't
worth a gold coin.

773
01:47:41,979 --> 01:47:44,279
Let Osman kill him.

774
01:47:44,477 --> 01:47:48,777
Dündar doesn't have any power or dignity.

775
01:47:48,884 --> 01:47:53,184
We'll see, Kalanoz.
We'll see.

776
01:47:54,354 --> 01:47:55,574
Helen.

777
01:47:55,943 --> 01:48:01,843
Go to Umur Bey and tell him
I want to meet him to talk about trade.

778
01:48:18,590 --> 01:48:22,840
- Can I come in, my Bey?
- Come in, brother.

779
01:48:28,793 --> 01:48:30,903
Tell me, brother.

780
01:48:31,358 --> 01:48:33,958
Did you see my uncle?

781
01:48:34,254 --> 01:48:38,254
Did you look into the traitor's eyes?
Tell me.

782
01:48:39,558 --> 01:48:42,358
I did, brother.

783
01:48:42,720 --> 01:48:48,150
He believes his own lie. He says
he will protect our tent from Geyhatu.

784
01:49:03,284 --> 01:49:06,324
He makes up excuses for his betrayal.

785
01:49:08,769 --> 01:49:10,619
What about Nikola?

786
01:49:10,931 --> 01:49:13,041
Did he accept the ransom?

787
01:49:13,483 --> 01:49:15,143
No.

788
01:49:16,329 --> 01:49:18,909
He has another trick, obviously.

789
01:49:20,191 --> 01:49:22,451
I'm sure he has.

790
01:49:23,087 --> 01:49:26,617
However, he should think that we have
no other choice than ransom.

791
01:49:27,697 --> 01:49:32,657
- He plays his trick according to that.
- Do we have another choice, Osman Bey?

792
01:49:32,717 --> 01:49:35,887
We don't have any spies in the Castle.

793
01:49:39,627 --> 01:49:42,227
We will get my uncle out of that Castle.

794
01:49:43,132 --> 01:49:47,962
We will take him from Nikola
and bring him to the tent.

795
01:50:18,798 --> 01:50:19,918
Umur Bey.

796
01:50:20,613 --> 01:50:23,403
Osman prevented our trade.

797
01:50:23,627 --> 01:50:27,957
However, he can't prevent our friendship.

798
01:50:29,788 --> 01:50:31,308
I'm happy about that.

799
01:50:31,563 --> 01:50:34,403
Osman is angry because he's desperate.

800
01:50:34,541 --> 01:50:37,721
Only the Beys like you can discipline him.

801
01:50:38,037 --> 01:50:41,297
We'll have peace by that.

802
01:50:41,392 --> 01:50:46,202
He is angrier this time, Nikola.

803
01:50:47,039 --> 01:50:51,919
He learned that
the traitor in the tent is Dündar Bey.

804
01:50:53,705 --> 01:50:56,205
And Dündar escaped.

805
01:50:56,599 --> 01:50:59,969
Who knows where he is hiding...

806
01:51:01,119 --> 01:51:03,835
He took shelter in the lands
of trade and peace...

807
01:51:03,945 --> 01:51:07,985
like you did, Umur Bey.

808
01:51:08,530 --> 01:51:09,790
What?

809
01:51:11,164 --> 01:51:15,744
- Is Dündar here?
- For now.

810
01:51:15,894 --> 01:51:20,204
Other Turks hate him too as Osman does.

811
01:51:20,403 --> 01:51:22,173
Then...

812
01:51:22,991 --> 01:51:25,451
stop the hate.

813
01:51:25,627 --> 01:51:29,027
- Send him to Osman.
- Umur Bey...

814
01:51:29,410 --> 01:51:32,860
I can see that you're wise.

815
01:51:32,949 --> 01:51:37,499
However, I am as wise as you.

816
01:51:38,861 --> 01:51:44,151
I want to do something to stop the
hostility between me and Osman.

817
01:51:44,217 --> 01:51:48,387
And I can give you power too
if I can do that.

818
01:51:50,655 --> 01:51:54,275
What are you thinking, Nikola?

819
01:51:55,273 --> 01:52:01,733
What happens if you give the traitor
to Osman?

820
01:52:02,155 --> 01:52:06,155
When you give him to Osman...

821
01:52:07,611 --> 01:52:10,711
he will think you are respected.

822
01:52:12,868 --> 01:52:16,918
Just him? No.

823
01:52:17,583 --> 01:52:21,083
All of the Beys will think the same.

824
01:52:21,335 --> 01:52:25,575
And your dignity will be my
biggest power, Umur Bey.

825
01:52:28,392 --> 01:52:30,682
What do you want in return for it?

826
01:52:30,802 --> 01:52:34,392
Osman offered me a thousand gold coins.

827
01:52:34,539 --> 01:52:38,079
If you offer me ten thousand gold coins...

828
01:52:38,411 --> 01:52:40,841
I will give you Dündar.

829
01:52:41,206 --> 01:52:46,806
So, the gold will be mine, the dignity
will be yours...

830
01:52:47,171 --> 01:52:50,721
and his blood will be Osman's.

831
01:53:14,321 --> 01:53:16,501
I will do everything I can.

832
01:53:16,546 --> 01:53:20,016
I love good agreements.

833
01:53:20,953 --> 01:53:23,013
You should join us for dinner.

834
01:53:23,109 --> 01:53:26,119
İnegöl needs new goods.

835
01:53:26,211 --> 01:53:31,041
We will talk again
when I come to take Dündar Bey.

836
01:53:31,201 --> 01:53:34,001
However you want, Umur Bey.

837
01:53:46,421 --> 01:53:49,311
However you want.

838
01:54:27,187 --> 01:54:29,117
Dündar Bey.

839
01:54:30,309 --> 01:54:32,319
A Turkmen Bey...

840
01:54:32,993 --> 01:54:36,683
shouldn't take shelter in the
enemy's place.

841
01:54:36,904 --> 01:54:41,064
Umur Bey, we have the same path.

842
01:54:41,570 --> 01:54:45,570
- The peace and the trade.
- Don't.

843
01:54:45,831 --> 01:54:49,111
Don't ever consider me equal to you!

844
01:54:50,637 --> 01:54:53,037
I sell goods.

845
01:54:53,579 --> 01:54:56,509
However, you sell your character.

846
01:54:57,546 --> 01:55:00,386
Shame on you!

847
01:55:00,585 --> 01:55:05,615
Don't criticize me!
Ever.

848
01:55:05,841 --> 01:55:11,931
The lands that
you are at will be mine soon.

849
01:55:11,972 --> 01:55:13,782
Don't forget.

850
01:55:14,277 --> 01:55:20,717
When that time comes, I will be
against you.

851
01:55:56,613 --> 01:55:59,483
I was with Nikola.

852
01:55:59,725 --> 01:56:04,315
We had a trade situation.
I went to talk about it.

853
01:56:06,363 --> 01:56:09,743
May Allah give you abundance, Umur Bey.

854
01:56:10,395 --> 01:56:11,695
I...

855
01:56:13,081 --> 01:56:15,341
saw Dündar Bey there.

856
01:56:16,453 --> 01:56:20,533
Sadly, I learned that the thumb ring...

857
01:56:21,875 --> 01:56:24,765
belonged to him.

858
01:56:27,344 --> 01:56:30,544
Good for you, then.

859
01:56:32,255 --> 01:56:36,775
Nikola wants ten thousand gold coins.

860
01:56:40,145 --> 01:56:41,945
Osman Bey...

861
01:56:42,005 --> 01:56:44,285
I can help if you want.

862
01:56:44,299 --> 01:56:50,229
You want to help because you didn't give
me the thumb ring on time.

863
01:56:52,239 --> 01:56:54,599
Don't worry, Umur Bey.

864
01:56:56,030 --> 01:56:58,170
We will figure it out.

865
01:56:58,414 --> 01:57:01,724
What about the friendship, Osman Bey?

866
01:57:03,688 --> 01:57:08,718
Tell me what I should do to stop
the hostility between us.

867
01:57:08,807 --> 01:57:13,977
- Do you want to be friends with us?
- Of course, Osman Bey.

868
01:57:18,653 --> 01:57:22,173
You came here in vain, Umur Bey.

869
01:57:22,475 --> 01:57:24,565
What you should do is...

870
01:57:26,134 --> 01:57:29,034
to stay out of my business.

871
01:57:33,374 --> 01:57:34,754
Now...

872
01:57:36,106 --> 01:57:38,446
go to your tent.

873
01:57:45,234 --> 01:57:47,934
Okay then, Osman Bey.

874
01:57:48,978 --> 01:57:51,078
Okay then.

875
01:58:05,376 --> 01:58:07,566
Baysungur.

876
01:58:09,976 --> 01:58:10,946
Yes, my Bey.

877
01:58:11,015 --> 01:58:13,385
Tell the Beys to come here.

878
01:58:24,964 --> 01:58:30,134
The miners will get to Söğüt by
using these tunnels.

879
01:58:30,395 --> 01:58:32,935
Will the Mongol fire blow out
at the same time?

880
01:58:32,990 --> 01:58:37,370
In the mosque, in the inn...

881
01:58:38,247 --> 01:58:40,727
and in the soup kitchen.
At the same time.

882
01:58:41,221 --> 01:58:44,361
I can't even think of the panic.

883
01:58:44,553 --> 01:58:51,383
Our union will come our of Petrus' shop
and will attack the Alps.

884
01:58:51,752 --> 01:58:57,292
I will take the archers and
cavalries. Then, I will attack.

885
01:58:57,358 --> 01:58:59,168
What about me?

886
01:58:59,244 --> 01:59:04,814
You will meet the troop when Osman gets
out of his tent with the Alps...

887
01:59:04,885 --> 01:59:11,715
and when the tent is left, you
will destroy there.

888
01:59:13,084 --> 01:59:16,224
It was wise of you to accept the ransom.

889
01:59:16,659 --> 01:59:20,659
It's the best excuse to stall Osman.

890
01:59:21,477 --> 01:59:23,397
What about Dündar?

891
01:59:24,329 --> 01:59:26,979
Dündar.

892
01:59:27,709 --> 01:59:30,019
When we are done here...

893
01:59:31,374 --> 01:59:34,724
you will be the person who
will kill him, Kalanoz.

894
01:59:42,373 --> 01:59:44,053
Nikola...

895
01:59:44,187 --> 01:59:47,797
is kidding with us or
he doesn't know how to count!

896
01:59:48,179 --> 01:59:51,119
This can't be a ransom, Osman Bey.

897
01:59:52,429 --> 01:59:54,839
He wants to weaken us.

898
01:59:55,009 --> 01:59:59,489
If we pay what he wants, we can't
fulfill the needs of the tent...

899
02:00:00,020 --> 02:00:02,040
...nor the expenditures of
the campaigns.

900
02:00:02,151 --> 02:00:08,041
And he will use the heathen's money
to feed the soldiers he'll use against us.

901
02:00:08,364 --> 02:00:12,084
He will surely do that, Davud Bey.

902
02:00:13,070 --> 02:00:14,740
If so...

903
02:00:15,319 --> 02:00:17,429
...if we can't give this ransom.

904
02:00:17,944 --> 02:00:19,784
Then we know what to do.

905
02:00:19,948 --> 02:00:24,968
We'll march to İnegöl and blow down
that castle upon Nikola and Dündar.

906
02:00:25,202 --> 02:00:28,602
There is nothing else we can do,
Osman Bey.

907
02:00:29,236 --> 02:00:32,786
My opinion about İnegöl Castle is
known, is it not?

908
02:00:33,138 --> 02:00:36,598
It is. It is.

909
02:00:36,717 --> 02:00:39,877
You think about sieging it.
Cutting its breath.

910
02:00:39,902 --> 02:00:43,462
And you think that we need
more alps.

911
02:00:43,932 --> 02:00:46,622
Otherwise, attacking the walls...

912
02:00:47,291 --> 02:00:49,941
...will give no result, right?

913
02:00:50,081 --> 02:00:55,161
Then, tell me how will we kill the
murderers of my son, Osman Bey!

914
02:00:56,485 --> 02:00:57,905
Nikola...

915
02:00:58,507 --> 02:01:02,777
...when he asked for Kulucahisar
for Bayhoca...

916
02:01:03,145 --> 02:01:05,875
...remember what we said.

917
02:01:05,956 --> 02:01:08,166
We remember it, Osman Bey.

918
02:01:08,290 --> 02:01:11,440
Some of us said that the lands
of the country can't be given.

919
02:01:11,440 --> 02:01:13,856
Some of us said that we should
save the Kayı bey.

920
02:01:17,564 --> 02:01:21,424
And what did I do?

921
02:01:22,221 --> 02:01:24,841
You saved Bayhoca.

922
02:01:25,783 --> 02:01:28,073
And you didn't give our castle.

923
02:01:30,173 --> 02:01:32,813
I will do the same now.

924
02:01:33,401 --> 02:01:37,401
I will take Dündar apart from that
castle.

925
02:01:38,796 --> 02:01:44,366
And I won't give a coin
to this dog called Nikola!

926
02:01:50,336 --> 02:01:52,876
I was suspicious of Dündar Bey.

927
02:01:52,962 --> 02:01:56,502
But I didn't expect this much.

928
02:01:56,840 --> 02:02:00,250
May Allah save everyone from
such curse.

929
02:02:00,432 --> 02:02:03,052
What will happen now, my bey?

930
02:02:03,127 --> 02:02:04,647
Now...

931
02:02:06,010 --> 02:02:09,760
...he has to pay the heavy ransom
that Nikola wants.

932
02:02:12,023 --> 02:02:15,293
As long as his treacherous uncle
lives...

933
02:02:15,497 --> 02:02:18,847
...he'll have no reputation among
the Turkmen tribes.

934
02:02:21,713 --> 02:02:23,733
Osman Bey...

935
02:02:31,300 --> 02:02:34,090
You look sad.

936
02:02:36,219 --> 02:02:39,619
Isn't that much burden too much
for a man, father?

937
02:02:41,544 --> 02:02:43,834
That's for Osman Bey to think.

938
02:02:44,858 --> 02:02:46,938
We'll think about our own burden.

939
02:02:46,993 --> 02:02:50,603
Osman Bey hoped for us to ease his burden.

940
02:02:50,798 --> 02:02:53,588
He had hopes for us.

941
02:02:56,718 --> 02:03:00,718
It's late, father.
Good night.

942
02:03:01,731 --> 02:03:03,971
Good night.

943
02:03:08,994 --> 02:03:12,484
Is this the thing I feared?

944
02:03:49,552 --> 02:03:51,512
Finally.

945
02:03:52,833 --> 02:03:55,743
You will kill us now.

946
02:03:58,898 --> 02:04:03,588
Our holy father in heaven...

947
02:04:21,188 --> 02:04:23,128
I thought that...

948
02:04:24,402 --> 02:04:27,382
...you will serve better...

949
02:04:27,616 --> 02:04:30,356
...alive than dead.

950
02:04:31,125 --> 02:04:35,125
Will you release us?

951
02:04:39,583 --> 02:04:42,653
What do you want in return.

952
02:04:47,538 --> 02:04:49,828
Dündar.

953
02:04:52,347 --> 02:04:54,797
You will stay here.

954
02:04:57,974 --> 02:05:01,684
You will go to İnegöl to meet with Nikola.

955
02:05:03,072 --> 02:05:06,302
You will meet Dündar in secret.

956
02:05:06,458 --> 02:05:11,588
And you will convince him to run away
to Constantinople.

957
02:05:11,860 --> 02:05:14,360
You will bring him to me.

958
02:05:14,550 --> 02:05:17,290
Even if I convince Nikola...

959
02:05:17,610 --> 02:05:21,000
...how will I convince Dündar Bey?

960
02:05:21,127 --> 02:05:22,657
I will let you know...

961
02:05:23,683 --> 02:05:26,973
...what to tell Nikola and Dündar.

962
02:05:28,861 --> 02:05:30,421
Me...

963
02:05:32,015 --> 02:05:34,735
...what will you do to me.

964
02:05:38,222 --> 02:05:40,992
If I get what I want.

965
02:05:43,267 --> 02:05:45,837
I will send you to the pope.

966
02:05:48,074 --> 02:05:51,474
And you will carry a letter from me.

967
02:05:54,366 --> 02:05:55,956
But...

968
02:05:57,400 --> 02:05:59,620
...if you fail...

969
02:05:59,773 --> 02:06:05,963
...I will personally send Petros'
head to the pope.

970
02:06:11,441 --> 02:06:14,141
We trust your word.

971
02:06:14,208 --> 02:06:16,908
If that's your offer.

972
02:06:17,293 --> 02:06:20,183
We are listening, Osman Bey.

973
02:06:22,891 --> 02:06:25,061
Good.

974
02:06:28,066 --> 02:06:31,246
Listen well, then.

975
02:06:37,906 --> 02:06:40,626
Nikola...
Nikola...

976
02:06:41,005 --> 02:06:45,005
So, Dündar Bey took refuge
under you.

977
02:06:45,286 --> 02:06:48,526
That was the best he could.

978
02:06:48,716 --> 02:06:52,996
Only his enemy can open his arms
to a traitor, right?

979
02:06:55,073 --> 02:07:00,203
Unfortunately, our most loyal spy
won't work now.

980
02:07:02,445 --> 02:07:05,215
We won't need him.

981
02:07:05,340 --> 02:07:10,860
When I take Söğüt, all the Turkish
hegemony in Bhytinia will end.

982
02:07:13,094 --> 02:07:16,794
It will be the end of Osman, Simon.

983
02:07:17,074 --> 02:07:19,374
It will be.

984
02:07:20,320 --> 02:07:23,660
Then, I should go and talk to Dündar.

985
02:07:24,446 --> 02:07:30,156
I wonder what will be the last crumbs
of information I will get from him.

986
02:07:34,532 --> 02:07:36,782
Where is Petros?

987
02:07:43,201 --> 02:07:47,711
He went to İznik to see the pope's helper.

988
02:07:49,351 --> 02:07:51,941
He'll be back in a few day.

989
02:07:52,954 --> 02:07:56,114
If you allow me, Lord Nikola.

990
02:08:21,587 --> 02:08:24,357
I heard what happened, Dündar Bey.

991
02:08:24,875 --> 02:08:27,715
Have you got any news from Hazal?

992
02:08:27,818 --> 02:08:31,778
Unfortunately. We have more important
problems than Hazal Hatun now.

993
02:08:31,843 --> 02:08:33,923
What happened to Hazal, I said!

994
02:08:34,060 --> 02:08:38,160
Osman Bey banished Hazal Hatun
from the tribe.

995
02:08:38,195 --> 02:08:40,725
He sent her to his brother.

996
02:08:47,631 --> 02:08:49,751
Oh, Hazal.

997
02:08:51,118 --> 02:08:53,138
Don't worry.

998
02:08:54,405 --> 02:08:59,015
When we take you to Constantinople,
Hazal Hatun will come with us.

999
02:08:59,214 --> 02:09:02,114
Petros arranged everything.

1000
02:09:03,620 --> 02:09:06,210
What does that mean?

1001
02:09:07,031 --> 02:09:12,481
I will stay here and fight for the
throne that I deserve.

1002
02:09:15,913 --> 02:09:19,913
Or, did you discard me?

1003
02:09:20,302 --> 02:09:22,652
Not us, Dündar Bey.

1004
02:09:22,702 --> 02:09:26,142
It is Nikola who discarded you.

1005
02:09:28,894 --> 02:09:31,414
What does that mean?

1006
02:09:31,720 --> 02:09:35,720
Nikola accepted the ransom that
Osman will pay for you.

1007
02:09:37,488 --> 02:09:39,978
This isn't possible.
It's not.

1008
02:09:40,121 --> 02:09:43,691
If you had heard the price that Osman
is willing to pay for you.

1009
02:09:43,819 --> 02:09:46,809
You would know that it's possible.

1010
02:09:54,107 --> 02:09:58,967
But it doesn't fit you to be daunted,
Dündar Bey.

1011
02:10:00,375 --> 02:10:02,555
We still need each other.

1012
02:10:04,890 --> 02:10:11,130
Even if Nikola betrays you for a bunch of
golds that Osman offers.

1013
02:10:12,666 --> 02:10:15,156
I will kill him!

1014
02:10:15,362 --> 02:10:19,112
I will kill him! I will kill him!

1015
02:10:19,271 --> 02:10:23,711
No. I can't get you out of
here if you do that.

1016
02:10:24,134 --> 02:10:27,834
Why are you endangering yourself for me?

1017
02:10:28,316 --> 02:10:31,656
If Nikola gives you to Osman...

1018
02:10:31,848 --> 02:10:35,038
it will be our end too.

1019
02:10:35,260 --> 02:10:40,590
And we still need a powerful
Bey like you...

1020
